        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "63b05f4a-6f52-52a4-8b20-840ebb990507",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Orgasm, A Hard Day's Night\n- People: Simon Napier-Bell, Richard Lester, John Lennon, Paul McCartney, George Harrison, Ringo Starr\n- Organizations: John's Children, the Beatles\n- Topics: album release history, fake live albums, film production\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, A Hard Day's Night was released as a British musical comedy film directed by Richard Lester and starring the Beatles: John Lennon, Paul McCartney, George Harrison, and Ringo Starr.\n- Orgasm is John's Children's only studio album.\n- Orgasm was projected for release on 18 March 1967.\n- Simon Napier-Bell transformed Orgasm from a regular studio album into a fake live album by dubbing in audience screams taken from A Hard Day's Night.\n- Orgasm was eventually released in September 1970.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d535fe5f-416e-54b1-ae03-1ae67bada135",
